   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning Objectives:** Understand convolution operations, pooling, CNN architecture, build CNNs for CIFAR-10, apply data augmentation, and visualize feature maps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. The Convolution Operation\n",
    "\n",
    "Convolution applies a **filter/kernel** across an input image, producing a **feature map**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each filter detects specific features (edges, textures, patterns). Early layers detect low-level features; deeper layers detect high-level features.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Mathematically:** $(I * K)_{i,j} = \\sum_{m} \\sum_{n} I_{i+m, j+n} \\cdot K_{m,n}$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Parameters:**\n",
    "| Parameter | Description | Effect |\n",
    "|-----------|-------------|--------|\n",
    "| **Filter size** | Height × width of kernel (e.g., 3×3, 5×7) | Larger = more context, more params |\n",
    "| **Stride** | Step size between applications | Larger = smaller output |\n",
    "| **Padding** | Zeros around input border | 'valid' = no padding, 'same' = output same size |\n",
    "| **Filters** | Number of kernels in the layer | More = more capacity"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Manual convolution (2D) for understanding\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "def conv2d_manual(image, kernel, padding='valid'):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Manually apply a 2D convolution.\"\"\"\n",
    "    h, w = image.shape\n",
    "    kh, kw = kernel.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "    if padding == 'same':\n",
    "        pad_h, pad_w = kh // 2, kw // 2\n",
    "        image = np.pad(image, ((pad_h, pad_h), (pad_w, pad_w)), mode='constant')\n",
    "        h, w = image.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "    out_h = h - kh + 1\n",
    "    out_w = w - kw + 1\n",
    "    output = np.zeros((out_h, out_w))\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i in range(out_h):\n",
    "        for j in range(out_w):\n",
    "            output[i, j] = np.sum(image[i:i+kh, j:j+kw] * kernel)\n",
    "    return output\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test with edge detection\n",
    "image = np.array([\n",
    "    [10, 10, 10, 0, 0],\n",
    "    [10, 10, 10, 0, 0],\n",
    "    [10, 10, 10, 0, 0],\n",
    "    [10, 10, 10, 0, 0],\n",
    "    [10, 10, 10, 0, 0]\n",
    "])\n",
    "sobel_x = np.array([[-1, 0, 1], [-2, 0, 2], [-1, 0, 1]])  # vertical edge detector\n",
    "\n",
    "result = conv2d_manual(image, sobel_x)\n",
    "print(\"Edge detection result:\")\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize convolution on an actual image\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from skimage import data, color\n",
    "\n",
    "camera = data.camera()\n",
    "kernel_sharpen = np.array([[0, -1, 0], [-1, 5, -1], [0, -1, 0]])\n",
    "kernel_edge = np.array([[-1, -1, -1], [-1, 8, -1], [-1, -1, -1]])\n",
    "\n",
    "sharpened = conv2d_manual(camera, kernel_sharpen, padding='same')\n",
    "edges = conv2d_manual(camera, kernel_edge, padding='same')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
    "axes[0].imshow(camera, cmap='gray')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Original')\n",
    "axes[1].imshow(sharpened, cmap='gray')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Sharpened')\n",
    "axes[2].imshow(edges, cmap='gray')\n",
    "axes[2].set_title('Edge Detection')\n",
    "for ax in axes:\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Pooling Layers\n",
    "\n",
    "Pooling reduces spatial dimensions, providing **translation invariance** and **computational efficiency**.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Type | Operation | Use Case |\n",
    "|------|-----------|----------|\n",
    "| **Max Pooling** | Take max in each window | Most common, preserves strong features |\n",
    "| **Average Pooling** | Take average in each window | Smooth features, GlobalAveragePooling |\n",
    "| **Global Pooling** | Pool entire feature map | Replace Flatten + Dense at end |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Build a CNN for CIFAR-10\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow import keras\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras import layers\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_cnn(input_shape=(32, 32, 3), num_classes=10):\n",
    "    model = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "        # Conv block 1\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(32, (3, 3), padding='same', activation='relu', input_shape=input_shape),\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(32, (3, 3), padding='same', activation='relu'),\n",
    "        layers.MaxPooling2D(2, 2),\n",
    "        layers.Dropout(0.25),\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Conv block 2\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(64, (3, 3), padding='same', activation='relu'),\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(64, (3, 3), padding='same', activation='relu'),\n",
    "        layers.MaxPooling2D(2, 2),\n",
    "        layers.Dropout(0.25),\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Conv block 3\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(128, (3, 3), padding='same', activation='relu'),\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(128, (3, 3), padding='same', activation='relu'),\n",
    "        layers.MaxPooling2D(2, 2),\n",
    "        layers.Dropout(0.25),\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Classifier\n",
    "        layers.Flatten(),\n",
    "        layers.Dense(256, activation='relu'),\n",
    "        layers.Dropout(0.5),\n",
    "        layers.Dense(num_classes, activation='softmax')\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    return model\n",
    "\n",
    "cnn_model = build_cnn()\n",
    "cnn_model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load and preprocess CIFAR-10\n",
    "(x_train, y_train), (x_test, y_test) = keras.datasets.cifar10.load_data()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Normalize\n",
    "x_train = x_train.astype('float32') / 255.0\n",
    "x_test = x_test.astype('float32') / 255.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# One-hot encode labels\n",
    "y_train_cat = keras.utils.to_categorical(y_train, 10)\n",
    "y_test_cat = keras.utils.to_categorical(y_test, 10)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train: {x_train.shape}, Test: {x_test.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show sample images with class names\n",
    "class_names = ['airplane', 'automobile', 'bird', 'cat', 'deer',\n",
    "               'dog', 'frog', 'horse', 'ship', 'truck']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 5, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "for i, ax in enumerate(axes.flat):\n",
    "    ax.imshow(x_train[i])\n",
    "    ax.set_title(class_names[y_train[i][0]])\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compile and train (use a small subset for speed)\n",
    "cnn_model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=0.001),\n",
    "    loss='categorical_crossentropy',\n",
    "    metrics=['accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "history = cnn_model.fit(\n",
    "    x_train, y_train_cat,\n",
    "    batch_size=64,\n",
    "    epochs=10,\n",
    "    validation_split=0.2,\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Evaluate\n",
    "test_loss, test_acc = cnn_model.evaluate(x_test, y_test_cat, verbose=0)\n",
    "print(f\"Test accuracy: {test_acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot training history\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "ax1.plot(history.history['loss'], label='Train Loss')\n",
    "ax1.plot(history.history['val_loss'], label='Val Loss')\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Loss')\n",
    "ax1.legend()\n",
    "ax1.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "ax2.plot(history.history['accuracy'], label='Train Acc')\n",
    "ax2.plot(history.history['val_accuracy'], label='Val Acc')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Accuracy')\n",
    "ax2.legend()\n",
    "ax2.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Data Augmentation with ImageDataGenerator\n",
    "\n",
    "Data augmentation artificially expands the dataset with random transformations, reducing overfitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Data augmentation pipeline\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.preprocessing.image import ImageDataGenerator\n",
    "\n",
    "datagen = ImageDataGenerator(\n",
    "    rotation_range=15,\n",
    "    width_shift_range=0.1,\n",
    "    height_shift_range=0.1,\n",
    "    horizontal_flip=True,\n",
    "    zoom_range=0.1,\n",
    "    brightness_range=(0.8, 1.2),\n",
    "    fill_mode='nearest'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize augmented images\n",
    "aug_iter = datagen.flow(x_train[:8], y_train_cat[:8], batch_size=8)\n",
    "aug_batch = next(aug_iter)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 4, figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "for i, ax in enumerate(axes.flat):\n",
    "    ax.imshow(aug_batch[0][i])\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Augmented CIFAR-10 Images')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train with data augmentation\n",
    "aug_model = build_cnn()\n",
    "aug_model.compile(optimizer='adam', loss='categorical_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "\n",
    "history_aug = aug_model.fit(\n",
    "    datagen.flow(x_train, y_train_cat, batch_size=64),\n",
    "    epochs=15,\n",
    "    validation_data=(x_test, y_test_cat),\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "test_acc_aug = aug_model.evaluate(x_test, y_test_cat, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "print(f\"Test accuracy with augmentation: {test_acc_aug:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. LeNet-5 Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "LeNet-5 (LeCun, 1998) was one of the first CNNs:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Layer | Type | Filters | Size | Activation |\n",
    "|-------|------|---------|------|------------|\n",
    "| C1 | Conv2D | 6 | 5×5 | Tanh |\n",
    "| S2 | Avg Pool | — | 2×2 | — |\n",
    "| C3 | Conv2D | 16 | 5×5 | Tanh |\n",
    "| S4 | Avg Pool | — | 2×2 | — |\n",
    "| C5 | Conv2D | 120 | 5×5 | Tanh |\n",
    "| F6 | Dense | 84 | — | Tanh |\n",
    "| Output | Dense | 10 | — | Softmax |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# LeNet-5 implementation in Keras\n",
    "def lenet5(input_shape=(32, 32, 1), num_classes=10):\n",
    "    model = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(6, (5, 5), activation='tanh', input_shape=input_shape, padding='same'),\n",
    "        layers.AveragePooling2D(2, 2),\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(16, (5, 5), activation='tanh'),\n",
    "        layers.AveragePooling2D(2, 2),\n",
    "        layers.Conv2D(120, (5, 5), activation='tanh'),\n",
    "        layers.Flatten(),\n",
    "        layers.Dense(84, activation='tanh'),\n",
    "        layers.Dense(num_classes, activation='softmax')\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    return model\n",
    "\n",
    "lenet = lenet5()\n",
    "lenet.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": {
    "## 5. Visualizing Filters and Feature Maps\n",
    "\n",
    "Understanding what CNNs learn by visualizing first-layer filters and intermediate feature maps."
   }
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize learned filters from first conv layer\n",
    "filters, _ = cnn_model.layers[0].get_weights()\n",
    "filters = (filters - filters.min()) / (filters.max() - filters.min())  # normalize\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(4, 8, figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "for i, ax in enumerate(axes.flat):\n",
    "    if i < 32:\n",
    "        ax.imshow(filters[:, :, :, i])\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
